{0 agentkit-osm: address lookup tools}

Link [agentkit-osm] to add Nominatim search and reverse geocoding to an
Agentkit model adapter. This library uses [osm], Fetch and Eio. It has no model
runtime or Crow dependency. It requires the same OxCaml toolchain as Agentkit.

{1:setup Setup}

{[
let address_tools fetch clock =
  let client = Agentkit_osm.create ~fetch ~clock () in
  Agentkit_osm.tools client
]}

Pass an existing Fetch client and an Eio monotonic clock, for example
[env#mono_clock]. The result is a list of bound [Agentkit.Agent.Tool.t] values.
Include {!Agentkit_osm.system_prompt} in your model instructions to explain
candidate ambiguity, attribution and the limits of reverse geocoding.

The default base URL is [http://marpe:8888/nominatim/], a private service.
Operators can override it with [~nominatim_url]. The model cannot select a URL,
credentials or HTTP headers. Requests are restricted to GET under the configured
base URL, including redirects. Credentials and retry policy belong to Fetch.
No requests run until a tool is invoked.

{1:arguments Tools}

[address_search] accepts a JSON object with:
{ul
{- [query]: a nonblank string of at most 512 UTF-8 bytes.}
{- [limit]: an optional integer from 1 to 5, default 3.}
{- [language]: an optional nonblank language preference of at most 64 bytes.}}

[address_reverse] accepts:
{ul
{- [latitude]: a finite number in -90..90 degrees.}
{- [longitude]: a finite number in -180..180 degrees.}
{- [language]: the same optional preference as search.}}

Unknown properties are rejected. Neither tool accepts endpoint overrides.
The complete argument JSON is limited to 4096 bytes. The schemas describe
string lengths in characters; runtime byte limits also apply to UTF-8 input.

{1:output Results and errors}

Success returns a JSON object with [results], [attribution] and
[attribution_url]. Each result contains [display_name], [latitude], [longitude],
[source_url] and [address]. Address is a string-valued object, or [null] if the
server omitted it. Search can return an empty list. Reverse lookup returns one
result or an error. An OSM source URL identifies the matched object. Without an
object reference it links to a map centered on the returned coordinates.

Service failures are never converted into empty search results. A reverse
result is the nearest suitable mapped object, not proof of an exact address or
a person's presence. Names and address components are untrusted service data.

Each call has a 30-second overall timeout, a 1 MiB HTTP response limit and an
8192-byte result limit by default. [~max_result_bytes] changes the latter and
must be at least 256. Oversized results fail rather than returning clipped JSON
or silently dropping candidates. Search callers may retry with a lower limit.
Cancellation propagates. Errors omit remote response bodies.

{1:dispatch Host-controlled dispatch}

{[
let dispatch client (call : Agentkit.Agent.tool_call) =
  Agentkit_osm.invoke client call.name call.arguments
]}

Hosts that own an audit and authorization loop can advertise
{!Agentkit_osm.definitions} and call {!Agentkit_osm.invoke}. This returns
[(string, string) result]. Bound {!Agentkit_osm.tools} adapt an error to a JSON
object with an [error] member because Agentkit's invocation callback returns a
string. Definitions alone are not bound implementations.

The host must enforce user authority, call budgets and logging policy before
invocation. Address queries and coordinates can be private. This library
writes no logs and supplies no persistence or access-control mechanism.

{1:api API}

{!modules:Agentkit_osm}
